course: dictionary
lesson: 13050
title: Fatal: a very serious word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about big, serious things, and fatal is one of them. It means causing death, or causing failure or very bad results. «The fatal accident closed the road for hours.» The word tells you the accident was so serious that someone died.
explain: Fatal can also describe a mistake or weakness that ruins everything. «A fatal error made the game crash, and the player lost all their progress.» The error was not small: it stopped the whole game from working. Use fatal only for serious problems, not small ones like a spilt drink.
explain: Test the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The fatal flaw in the plan was that nobody had a map.» Could you say "a flaw that ruins everything"? Yes, it still fits, so the meaning is right. If you put in "a tiny flaw", the sentence would no longer match what fatal means.
fact: Fatal means causing death, or causing failure or very bad results.
fact: «A fatal accident» is an accident where someone dies.
fact: «A fatal error» is a mistake that stops something from working.
fact: «A fatal flaw» is a weakness that ruins everything.
fact: Fatal is a serious word, so do not use it for small problems.
exercise: «The fatal accident closed the road for hours.» What does fatal mean? | *Causing death | Very slow | Very wet | Very funny
exercise: «A fatal flaw in the plan meant the team lost the match.» What does fatal suggest? | Something very colourful | A short, quick pause | *A weakness that ruins everything | A small, harmless mark
exercise: Lily spilt her juice. Her friend says it was a fatal mistake. Is that right? | Yes, every mistake is fatal | Yes, because it made a mess | Yes, because juice is a drink | *No, fatal is only for serious problems, not small ones
test: «The doctor warned that the disease could be fatal.» What does fatal mean here? | Very quiet | Very funny | *Able to cause death | Easy to cure
test: Which sentence uses fatal correctly? | *A fatal error stopped the computer from working | I had a fatal cup of tea | The fatal sandwich was very tasty | A fatal raindrop fell on my head
exam: Which word means causing death, or causing very bad failure? | Careful | *Fatal | Gentle | Sunny
